# Taskmark project memory

If `taskmark/` exists in any workspace folder, treat Taskmark as the source of truth for planned, in-flight, and done product work.

1. **Multi-repo:** When the workspace has multiple folders / git repositories and the user is developing across them with AI, ensure **every** git project has a full copy of `taskmark/` (run `sync-taskmark-repos` at session start and after board edits). Do not keep the board in only one repo.
2. Before implementing a feature, bugfix, or product refactor: search the board for a matching epic/story/task/bug and **link work to it**.
3. If none exists and the work is real product scope, **create** items (`create-epic` / `create-story` / `create-task`) — no orphan product changes without a board trail.
4. When planning a new iteration, read `INDEX.md`, **Prompt & feedback** logs, and **Commits** so prior decisions and shipped work carry forward.
5. On each user turn tied to an item: append prompt/feedback, manage Work log (`start-work` / `complete-work`), **log commits** for touched repos, then implement; run `sync-status` after AC or session changes.
6. Never invent a parallel todo list in chat; update markdown under `taskmark/` instead, then propagate copies across linked repos.

If `taskmark/` is missing and the user wants structured planning, offer `taskmark-init` (then `sync-taskmark-repos` for multi-root).
